  for for workers particularly in gig  economy style  practices um really in terms of the  exact extent of what this is going to  mean  for companies is really hard hard to  predict  the indications are that deliveries so  called retail investors have chosen to  hang on to the stock instead of dumping  it  and the share price rose by a modest two  percent in early trading on wednesday  the liver hasn't yet published financial  results for 2020  and the apparent boom in the delivery  business during the pandemic year could  well bounce the share price back  up but the workers who made that  possible are demanding their share  of the success paul brennan al jazeera  shoreditch  east london
 

